# .dxtignore — what the DXT bundle must NOT carry.
#
# `dxt pack` bundles from the FILESYSTEM, git-agnostically: it does not read
# .gitignore at all. So everything .gitignore excludes still went into the
# bundle, and 2.4.0's `.dxt` was 27.4 MB of the 28.5 MB tarball — 100 MB of
# node_modules unpacked, including the TypeScript compiler and Prettier.
#
# Runtime dependencies MUST stay: a DXT bundle has no install step, so
# `node_modules` is how the server gets `better-sqlite3`, `sqlite-vec`, the MCP
# SDK and the rest at runtime. Only the things that exist to BUILD the package
# are excluded here.

# ---- devDependencies: present to build, never to run ----
node_modules/typescript
node_modules/ts-node
node_modules/@types
node_modules/@anthropic-ai/dxt
node_modules/@changesets
node_modules/prettier

# ---- sources: the bundle runs `build/`, it never compiles ----
src
e2e
eval
scripts
tsconfig*.json
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- repository furniture ----
.changeset
.github
.serena
.vscode
test
docs

# ---- tests and their compiled output (npm tarball excludes these separately;
#      the bundle inherited 58 of them into the .dxt as well) ----
*.test.js
*.test.d.ts
__mocks__
